  "goal": "Find the bakery.",
  "desired_behaviour": "The agent should call plan_route first, and it should be SHOWN the whole\nset of unexplored exits rather than one.\nIt should then choose from that set by reading the names — four of the\nfive exits out of the temple are parts of the temple itself (an altar, a\ndonation room, a reading room), and \"The Temple Square\" is the only one\nthat opens onto a city. A bakery is a shop and shops are on streets.\nChoosing a nearer exit BECAUSE it is nearer, when its name says it leads\ndeeper into a building, is the specific reasoning failure this case is\nwatching for.\nOnce it recognises the place it is walking through, calling\nname_region(region: \"Midgaard\") is correct and worth doing, though the\nbakery can be found without it.\n",
